= Scholarly communication — Technical =

A scholarly-communication system includes production, certification, registration, dissemination, discovery, archiving, and reuse functions. Digital infrastructures can separate these functions across publishers, repositories, identifier registries, indexing services, and community platforms.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* scholarly communication ≠ academic publishing only
* communication ≠ validation
* dissemination ≠ preservation

== References ==
* UNESCO, ''Recommendation on Open Science'' (2021).
* Christine L. Borgman, ''Scholarship in the Digital Age'' (2007), scholarly communication and digital research infrastructure.
* Crossref and DataCite documentation, for scholarly metadata, persistent links, and research-output relationships.
